60;2,705/2025. </div> <div style="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:9pt; font-family:ARIAL;text-align:justify">On January&#160;13, 2026, after the fulfillment of the closing conditions by YPF and TI, the transfer of 100% of the rights and obligations of YPF in such exploitation concessions in favor of TI was formalized. In addition, YPF and TI signed (i)&#160;a transitory operation agreement for the assigned exploitation concessions, pursuant to which YPF shall continue to operate said concessions for a maximum period of up to 3 months, and (ii)&#160;a service agreement for the Cruz del Sur Terminal. </div> <div style="margin-top:6pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:9pt; font-family:ARIAL;text-align:justify"><div style="text-decoration: underline; letter-spacing: 0px; top: 0px;display:inline;">The assignment and/or reversion agreements signed by YPF, which are subject to the fulfillment of closing conditions, including applicable regulatory and provincial approvals are described below</div>: </div> <div style="font-size:6pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt">&#160;</div>
